8,"Palawano, Central Language (PLC)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/plc/,"Central Palawano is a stable indigenous language of the Philippines. It belongs to the Austronesian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community.","Palawano, Central",Austronesian
9,"Palawan | Palawano Language, People, Culture, General Information",https://palawano.com/,"Palawano belongs to the Austronesian language family, within the Palawanic subgroup, and includes several varieties such as Brooke’s Point Palawano, Quezon Palawano, and Bugsuk Palawano.","Palawano, Central",Austronesian
